    ## Amendment (Oracle, 2026-11-19): the C1 test is a scheduling flake
    I read `crates/bboxy450-harness/src/dream/c1.rs:5996-6031`. The test waits a fixed **100 ms of wall time** for the spawned thread to publish `Phase::Paused`. Machine load is 10–14 on 10 cores (`uptime`), so the thread can simply not run within 100 ms. The property under test is "the pause is never dropped by a saturated lane", and the 100 ms is only a guard against hanging.
    - **Authorized:** raise that guard to 10 s, in the same harness commit series, with a comment stating that the bound guards against hangs and is not a latency claim. A dropped pause never shows up, so the test still fails, just at 10 s. Do not change the assertion or the production code. Apply the same fix to any sibling test in `c1.rs` that fails on the same kind of sub-second wall-clock window during your landing.
    - Then rerun the harness landing, bump the harness pin and run `make land` in term.


